<title>DENMARK: CYCLING-LOMBARDI WINS SECOND STAGE OF DENMARK TOUR.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-LOMBARDI WINS SECOND STAGE OF DENMARK TOUR.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Giovanni Lombardi of Italy won the 169 km second stage of the Tour of Denmark cycling race between Ribe and Soenderborg on Thursday.</p>
<p>Robbie McEwen of Australia, who came second in the first two stages, took over the yellow jersey as overall leader from Italy's Nicola Minali.</p>
<p>The 859 km race, with 96 participants, ends in Copenhagen on August 10.</p>
</text>
